From 40a8f7baf1e7e6526dd36c41563225527b8c850d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:26:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [physics] THE FLIP: the new weather becomes the game's
 default, with one opt-out, ?weather=old

To be applied once the clouds lane passes review (the coordinator, 24 Nov), on top of the look director's storms hook
(look-director 1de2bf6).
- physics/wx2.js: in a page every switch of the new weather is on unless the address turns it off; ?weather=old turns
  them all off (the weather as it was at v37, to the last digit); ?rainmap stays off (its effect is too small to see);
  where there is no page (the Node tests) every switch is off as before.
- render/kitmat.js (the rain streak's pale) and audio/audio.js (thunder by distance) read the same: on unless ?weather=old.
- world/index.js: the storms' hook fetches wx2.js and storms.js in the oil look unless ?weather=old.
- core/bench.js: the row 'weather: the old weather (?weather=old)', the new weather as a whole against the old, live.
The guard is already on design-weather (ade2f6f): a weather program that does not compile switches itself off.
CHECKED in the game in the headless browser: with no switches in the address every switch is on but rainmap, the
storms are loaded, the wind and cloud maps run, no errors, the picture draws; with ?weather=old every switch is off and
storms.js is never fetched. Suites (Node, where the switches stay off): physics 442, world and looks 103, unit 328
(one physics run of four had one failure that did not come back in the next three: a timing budget while the
headless browser was busy).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R5Bri2bBgFSfCmxpKKuURT
